  "body": "**What happens:** `crates/app/tests/trochoid_law.rs` (#1593, merged with PR #1597) places its 40 x 40 x 8 box stock at `pos (-20, -20, 0)` for the aligned case and at `pos (20, -20, 0)` with a quarter turn for the turned case. Its comment says the box \"lands on [-20, 20]^2 again\". A box stock stands **centred** on its place, so the aligned stock is on [-40, 0]^2 and the turned one on [0, 40] x [-40, 0]: each covers one quarter of the part ([-20, 20]^2).\n\nMeasured while writing `keep_law.rs` for #1603: `SetStock` of a 50 x 50 box at `pos (-25, -25, 0)` gives `stock_world_aabb_for` = (-50, -50) .. (0, 0).\n\n**Effect:** the suite's verdicts still hold (the op-level gouges do not read the stock), but the aligned-stock rows are weaker than they read: the program sim judges a quarter of the part, and \"a legal slot posts on the aligned stock\" is posted against a stock that does not hold the part. `engrave_law.rs` and `keep_law.rs` (PR for #1595 / #1603) place the stock at the origin and assert its bounds.\n\n**Done means:** `trochoid_law.rs`'s `job()` places the stock centred over the part on both cases (pos at the origin; the quarter turn keeps the footprint), asserts the stock's bounds, the comment is corrected, and the suite still passes. Check `circular_pick_law.rs` / `circular_entity_law.rs` for the same placement.\n\nRelated: #1593, #1603.\n",
